## 3. The design effects (pre-registered: v1.md sections 5 and 7; from scores.json)
  S3:invalid       design effect 5.62: rate 0.998, 95% CI at n/deff 0.991-1.000 (n 4685)
  S5:null          design effect 5.28: rate 0.041, 95% CI at n/deff 0.024-0.064 (n 2252)
  S3:null          design effect 4.74: rate 0.917, 95% CI at n/deff 0.873-0.950 (n 1075)
  S3c:effect:E1    design effect 1.54: rate 0.972, 95% CI at n/deff 0.913-0.995 (n 141)
  the false-SUPPORTED cells (S1, S2): largest design effect 1.0549 (S1:N5)
  S1 N1 at its design effect 1.0000: P(pass | sound) 0.9824, P(pass | doubled) 0.0465
  S1 N2 at its design effect 1.0000: P(pass | sound) 1.0000, P(pass | doubled) 1.0000
  S1 N5 at its design effect 1.0549: P(pass | sound) 0.9797, P(pass | doubled) 0.0509
  S1 N6c at its design effect 1.0000: P(pass | sound) 0.9824, P(pass | doubled) 0.0465
  S1 N8 at its design effect 1.0000: P(pass | sound) 0.9824, P(pass | doubled) 0.0465
  (N2's design effect is 1 + 1.6e-15; oc.error_rule_deff then takes a beta-binomial in which scipy
   overflows and reads 1.0 / 1.0; at a design effect of 1 the values are N1's)

